1
00:00:02,212 --> 00:00:07,355
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ Madinan Period Volume 2,

2
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:09,676
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:13,066
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:13,485 --> 00:00:19,091
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:19,115 --> 00:00:23,808
Dear brothers and sisters ألسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته.

6
00:00:24,509 --> 00:00:28,818
Al-Imam Ahmad(ألاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) narrates with an authentic chain of narration,

7
00:00:29,597 --> 00:00:31,128
عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ

8
00:00:31,262 --> 00:00:37,831
قَالَ : لَمَّا أَعْطَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَا أَعْطَى مِنْ ذلْكَ الْعَطَايَا فِي قُرَيْشٍ وَقَبَائِلِ الْعَرَبِ

9
00:00:38,406 --> 00:00:43,741
 وَلَمْ يَكُنْ فِي الْأَنْصَارِ مِنْهَا شَيْءٌ وَجَدَ هَذَا الْحَيُّ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ

10
00:00:44,057 --> 00:00:51,460
حَتَّى كَثُرَتْ فِيهِمُ الْقَالَةُ حَتَّى قَالَ قَائِلُهُمْ : لَقِيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَوْمَهُ

11
00:00:52,021 --> 00:00:54,757
فَدَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ سَعْدُ بْنُ عُبَادَةَ ،

12
00:00:54,797 --> 00:01:00,093
 فَقَالَ : يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ، إِنَّ هَذَا الْحَيَّ قَدْ وَجَدُوا عَلَيْكَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ

13
00:01:00,423 --> 00:01:07,890
لِمَا صَنَعْتَ فِي هَذَا الْفَيْءِ الَّذِي أَصَبْتَ ، قَسَمْتَ فِي قَوْمِكَ ، وَأَعْطَيْتَ عَطَايَا عِظَامًا فِي قَبَائِلِ الْعَرَبِ

14
00:01:08,050 --> 00:01:10,583
وَلَمْ يَكُن فِي هَذَا الْحَيِّ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ شَيْءٌ ،

15
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:13,423
قَالَ : فَأَيْنَ أَنْتَ مِنْ ذَلِكَ يَا سَعْدُ ؟

16
00:01:13,703 --> 00:01:17,073
قَالَ : يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ، مَا أَنَا إِلَّا امْرُؤٌ مِنْ قَوْمِي ،

17
00:01:17,303 --> 00:01:19,779
قَالَ : فَاجْمَعْ لِي قَوْمَكَ فِي هَذِهِ الْحَظِيرَةِ

18
00:01:20,148 --> 00:01:23,509
قَالَ : فَخَرَجَ سَعْدٌ ، فَجَمَعَ الْناسَ فِي تِلْكَ الْحَظِيرَةِ ،

19
00:01:23,803 --> 00:01:28,994
قَالَ : فَجَاءَ رِجَالٌ مِنَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ ، فَتَرَكَهُمْ ، فَدَخَلُوا وَجَاءَ آخَرُونَ ، فَرَدَّهُمْ

20
00:01:29,675 --> 00:01:35,125
 فَلَم يجْتَمَعُوا أَتَاهُ سَعْدٌ فَقَالَ : قَدِ اجْتَمَعَ لَكَ هَذَا الْحَيُّ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ

21
00:01:35,426 --> 00:01:40,995
قَالَ : فَأَتَاهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ ، بِالَّذِي هُوَ لَهُ أَهْلٌ

22
00:01:41,617 --> 00:01:49,214
ثُمَّ قَالَ : يَا مَعْشَرَ الْأَنْصَارِ مَا قَالَةٌ بَلَغَتْنِي عَنْكُمْ وَجِدَةٌ وَجَدْتُمُوهَا فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ ،

23
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:51,952
 أَلَمْ آتِكُمْ ضُلَّالًا فَهَدَاكُمُ اللَّهُ ؟

24
00:01:52,274 --> 00:01:57,427
وَعَالَةً فَأَغْنَاكُمُ اللَّهُ ؟ وَأَعْدَاءً فَأَلَّفَ اللَّهُ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِكُمْ ؟ ،

25
00:01:57,673 --> 00:02:01,016
 قَالُوا : بَلِ اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَمَنُّ وَأَفْضَلُ

26
00:02:01,192 --> 00:02:04,341
قَالَ : أَلَا تُجِيبُونَنِي يَا مَعْشَرَ الْأَنْصَارِ

27
00:02:04,516 --> 00:02:09,349
 قَالُوا : وَبِمَاذَا نُجِيبُكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ، وَلِلَّهِ وَلِرَسُولِهِ الْمَنُّ وَالْفَضْلُ

28
00:02:09,711 --> 00:02:23,045
قَالَ : أَمَا وَاللَّهِ لَوْ شِئْتُمْ لَقُلْتُمْ فَلَصَدَقْتُمْ وَصُدِّقْتُمْ ، أَتَيْتَنَا مُكَذَّبًا فَصَدَّقْنَاكَ ، وَمَخْذُولًا فَنَصَرْنَاكَ ، وَطَرِيدًا فَآوَيْنَاكَ ، وَعَائِلًا فَآغنَيْنَاكَ

29
00:02:23,367 --> 00:02:31,752
أَوَجَدْتُمْ فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ يَا مَعْشَرَ الْأَنْصَارِ فِي لُعَاعَةٍ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا ، تَأَلَّفْتُ بِهَا قَوْمًا لِيُسْلِمُوا ، وَوَكَلْتُكُمْ إِلَى إِسْلَامِكُمْ ؟

30
00:02:32,163 --> 00:02:40,024
أَفَلَا تَرْضَوْنَ يَا مَعْشَرَ الْأَنْصَارِ أَنْ يَذْهَبَ النَّاسُ بِالشَّاةِ وَالْبَعِيرِ ، وَتَرْجِعُونَ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  فِي رِحَالِكُمْ ؟

31
00:02:40,301 --> 00:02:51,416
فَوَالَّذِي نَفْسُ مُحَمَّدٍ بِيَدِهِ لَوْلَا الْهِجْرَةُ لَكُنْتُ امْرَأً مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ ، وَلَوْ سَلَكَ النَّاسُ شِعْبًا ، وَسَلَكَتِ الْأَنْصَارُ شِعْبًا لَسَلَكْتُ شِعْبَ الْأَنْصَارِ

32
00:02:51,944 --> 00:02:56,744
اللَّهُمَّ ارْحَمِ الْأَنْصَارَ ، وَأَبْنَاءَ الْأَنْصَارِ ، وَأَبْنَاءَ أَبْنَاءِ الْأَنْصَارِ

33
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:00,088
قَالَ : فَبَكَى الْقَوْمُ ، حَتَّى أَخْضَلُوا لِحَاهُمْ ،

34
00:03:00,279 --> 00:03:08,279
وَقَالُوا : رَضِينَا بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ قِسْمًا وَحَظًّا ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَتَفَرَّقُوا

35
00:03:08,853 --> 00:03:11,148
This is a narration by Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) and it's authentic

36
00:03:11,285 --> 00:03:15,768
and there's also equivalent narrations with some changes in the wordings

37
00:03:16,186 --> 00:03:18,658
by Al-Bukhari(ألبخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم) and other books of Hadith(حديث)

38
00:03:18,966 --> 00:03:23,072
and it is narrated by Abu Saeed Al-Khudari(أبوسعيد ألخدري). He said;

39
00:03:23,584 --> 00:03:33,171
When Rasool Allah ﷺ gave, out the spoils of Hunain(حنين) to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), and the Arab tribes.

40
00:03:33,713 --> 00:03:38,207
You see, the spoils of war of Hunain(حنين) were huge,

41
00:03:38,484 --> 00:03:44,963
because remember, Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف) took everything with him, women, children, and livestock.

42
00:03:45,513 --> 00:03:50,844
So, it was all there, as soon as they fled the Muslims took everything with them.

43
00:03:50,868 --> 00:03:55,224
It was a huge amount of camels and goats and sheep.

44
00:03:56,017 --> 00:04:00,576
Rasool Allah ﷺ just finished from Fateh Makkah(فتح مكه).

45
00:04:01,012 --> 00:04:06,819
And he has a large army with him, that includes people, who came for the first time.

46
00:04:07,245 --> 00:04:12,574
Some of these Arab tribes from outside Madina and the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

47
00:04:12,992 --> 00:04:15,142
I mean, for the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) this was the first time

48
00:04:15,182 --> 00:04:19,619
and for some of the other tribes their involvement in Ghazoo(غزؤ) was rare,

49
00:04:20,111 --> 00:04:27,840
but because this was a major expedition Rasool Allah ﷺ mobilized all of the Muslims to join him.

50
00:04:28,734 --> 00:04:38,554
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ started giving out from the spoils of war to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), and to the other Arab tribes.

51
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:42,455
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave Safwaan Ibn Ummayyah(صفوان إبن أمية) from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

52
00:04:42,835 --> 00:04:47,860
and he gave people like a Aqrah Bin Habis(ألأقره بن حابس), and Uyainah Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن)

53
00:04:48,161 --> 00:04:51,094
these are leaders of some of the Bedouin tribes.

54
00:04:51,434 --> 00:04:56,243
And he gave Al-Abbas Bin Mardaas(ألعباس بن مرداس), who was the head of the tribe of Bannu Sulaim(بنو سليم).

55
00:04:57,286 --> 00:05:03,917
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave everyone, and he only left out one tribe, and that tribe, is Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

56
00:05:04,461 --> 00:05:11,049
So, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) the ones who fled, were given, and the ones who fought went empty handed.

57
00:05:11,882 --> 00:05:15,480
And the Ansaar(أنْصَار), were saddened by that,

58
00:05:15,686 --> 00:05:22,916
I mean in the time of fighting Rasool Allah ﷺ calls us and then the time of giving, he gives someone else.

59
00:05:23,264 --> 00:05:27,735
We were the ones, whom Rasool Allah ﷺ called

60
00:05:28,021 --> 00:05:34,211
when Rasool Allah ﷺ was standing and everybody else was running away,

61
00:05:34,354 --> 00:05:35,892
who did Rasool Allah ﷺ called for.?

62
00:05:35,916 --> 00:05:36,321
He said;

63
00:05:36,361 --> 00:05:37,186
يا للانصار ,

64
00:05:37,281 --> 00:05:39,260
He told Al-Abbas(العباس), call the Ansaar(أنْصَار).

65
00:05:39,311 --> 00:05:40,670
And then he told them: Call Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج).

66
00:05:40,734 --> 00:05:46,302
So, these are the ones who came to fight, and were injured, and were killed.

67
00:05:46,675 --> 00:05:50,382
And now, when it's time to split the Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

68
00:05:50,691 --> 00:05:54,286
Rasool Allah ﷺ is giving everyone but them.

69
00:05:55,206 --> 00:06:01,642
So, there was some talk going on, among the Ansaar رضي الله عنهم, and they were sad by this and

70
00:06:02,349 --> 00:06:07,663
their leaders Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عبادة), had to go to Rasool Allah ﷺ and bring up the issue.

71
00:06:08,535 --> 00:06:10,490
So, he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

72
00:06:10,751 --> 00:06:19,000
یا رسول اللہ إِنَّ هَذَا الْحَيَّ قَدْ وَجَدُوا عَلَيْكَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ لِمَا صَنَعْتَ فِي هَذَا الْفَيْءِ الَّذِي أَصَبْتَ

73
00:06:19,024 --> 00:06:25,707
قَسَمْتَ فِي قَوْمِكَ ، وَأَعْطَيْتَ عَطَايَا عِظَامًا فِي قَبَائِلِ الْعَرَبِ ، وَلَمْ يَكُن فِي هَذَا الْحَيِّ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ شَيْءٌ

74
00:06:26,071 --> 00:06:30,660
O Messenger of Allah, these people, the Ansaar(انصار), are sad

75
00:06:31,025 --> 00:06:35,761
because you have given your people

76
00:06:36,206 --> 00:06:42,015
and you have given great portions, to the leaders of the Arab tribes.

77
00:06:42,039 --> 00:06:44,828
For example Al-Aqraa(الاقراه) was given 100 camels and

78
00:06:45,096 --> 00:06:48,772
Uyeynaa(عيينه) a 100 camels and then Al-Abbas Bin Mardaas(ألعباس بن مرداس) was given 50

79
00:06:49,128 --> 00:06:50,895
but then it was raised to 100.

80
00:06:51,579 --> 00:06:57,063
And these are يعني hundred camels يعني a camel is very expensive,

81
00:06:57,103 --> 00:07:02,953
so 100 camels is a big portion that is it's such a great amount of wealth.

82
00:07:03,522 --> 00:07:05,327
وَلَمْ يَكُن فِي هَذَا الْحَيِّ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ شَيْءٌ ،

83
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:06,846
And the Ansaar(أنْصَار) are empty handed.

84
00:07:06,974 --> 00:07:09,989
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عبادة), he told him

85
00:07:10,554 --> 00:07:11,952
فَأَيْنَ أَنْتَ مِنْ ذَلِكَ؟

86
00:07:12,253 --> 00:07:14,634
Where do you stand, O Saad(سعد)?

87
00:07:15,099 --> 00:07:17,634
Saad Ibn Ubadah رضي الله عنه said;

88
00:07:18,185 --> 00:07:21,798
يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ، مَا أَنَا إِلَّا امْرُؤٌ مِنْ قَوْمِي

89
00:07:22,091 --> 00:07:23,996
I am but I man from my people.

90
00:07:24,859 --> 00:07:30,355
That's a very intelligent way of saying that, I have, same question to ask?

91
00:07:31,055 --> 00:07:33,030
He is saying but I'm but one man from my people,

92
00:07:33,054 --> 00:07:36,737
he came and presented to Rasool Allah ﷺ the opinion of his people

93
00:07:36,761 --> 00:07:38,704
and when Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Where do you stand.?

94
00:07:38,744 --> 00:07:40,574
He said: I am but a man from my people.

95
00:07:41,174 --> 00:07:42,516
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

96
00:07:42,802 --> 00:07:44,977
قَالَ: فَاجْمَعْ لِي قَوْمَكَ فِي هَذِهِ الْحَظِيرَةِ ،

97
00:07:45,403 --> 00:07:47,998
Bring all of your people together in this pavilion.

98
00:07:48,401 --> 00:07:51,293
قَالَ : فَخَرَجَ سَعْدٌ ، فَجَمَعَ الْأَنْصَارَ فِي تِلْكَ الْحَظِيرَةِ ،

99
00:07:51,726 --> 00:07:59,014
Saad Ibn Ubadah رضي الله عنه went and gathered the Ansaar(أنْصَار) in the appointed pavilion.

100
00:07:59,229 --> 00:08:02,971
فَجَاءَ رِجَالٌ مِنَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ ، فَتَرَكَهُمْ ، فَدَخَلُوا وَجَاءَ آخَرُونَ ، فَرَدَّهُمْ ،

101
00:08:02,996 --> 00:08:05,526
and they were allowed to come in,

102
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:08,440
and while some others came and Rasool Allah ﷺ turned them back.

103
00:08:08,464 --> 00:08:10,186
This is a special meeting for Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار),

104
00:08:10,329 --> 00:08:15,817
 but he did allow some of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), who were his advisors and some important people to come in,

105
00:08:15,841 --> 00:08:18,153
but the rest were prevented from entering.

106
00:08:18,423 --> 00:08:21,307
This is a private meeting between Rasool Allah ﷺ, and the Ansaar(أنْصَار).

107
00:08:22,178 --> 00:08:26,425
فَلَمَّا اجْتَمَعُوا أَتَاهُ سَعْدٌ فَقَالَ : قَدِ اجْتَمَعَ لَكَ هَذَا الْحَيُّ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ ،

108
00:08:27,085 --> 00:08:32,250
When they were all there Rasool Allah ﷺ was told by Saad(سعد), the Ansaar(أنْصَار) have gathered.

109
00:08:32,622 --> 00:08:39,212
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ came, and the gathering was all ready, everybody was there before Rasool Allah ﷺ.

110
00:08:39,252 --> 00:08:43,970
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ came in and they were all in the tent or the pavilion.

111
00:08:44,506 --> 00:08:46,367
فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ ،

112
00:08:46,762 --> 00:08:49,388
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ praised Allah, and thanked Him.

113
00:08:49,751 --> 00:08:54,648
And that is how, we should start our major events, our talks,

114
00:08:54,949 --> 00:08:59,108
we start them, by praising Allahعَزّوجَلّ, that is the Sunnah(سنة).

115
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:05,325
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ spoke to the Ansaar(أنْصَار), these words.

116
00:09:05,743 --> 00:09:13,145
He said: Didn't I come to you and you were misguided and Allah guided you through me.?

117
00:09:13,923 --> 00:09:19,006
I came to you, when you were poor and Allah enriched you through me.?

118
00:09:19,377 --> 00:09:24,299
I came to you and you're enemies, and Allah brought you together.?

119
00:09:25,241 --> 00:09:28,974
They responded and said: All favors belong to Allah and His Messenger

120
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:32,036
everything that Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We agree.

121
00:09:32,258 --> 00:09:36,074
And all of these favors that you mentioned they belong to Allah and to you.

122
00:09:36,532 --> 00:09:40,419
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them. Well, won't you answer back.?

123
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:45,657
They said: What should we say,? When all favors belong to Allah, and His Messenger.!

124
00:09:46,083 --> 00:09:48,486
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: In the name of Allah.

125
00:09:48,870 --> 00:09:53,415
If you want, you may say, and you would be telling the truth if you do,

126
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:57,524
you came to us rejected, and we believed in you.!

127
00:09:57,708 --> 00:10:00,630
You were betrayed and we supported you.

128
00:10:00,846 --> 00:10:04,288
You were refugitive, and we provided you with the home.

129
00:10:04,392 --> 00:10:07,034
You were poor, and we enriched you.

130
00:10:07,313 --> 00:10:10,392
O, people of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار), Are you upset,

131
00:10:10,622 --> 00:10:20,061
because of a small material gain that I am using to bring, a people closer to Islam, while I have entrusted you to your Islam.!

132
00:10:20,659 --> 00:10:26,799
Aren't you content O people of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار), That people would go back with sheep and camels

133
00:10:27,072 --> 00:10:30,410
while you would go back to your homes with Rasool Ullah.

134
00:10:30,828 --> 00:10:34,503
In the name of whom Muhammad(محمد)'s soul is in His hands.

135
00:10:34,574 --> 00:10:39,105
If it wasn't for Hijrah(هجرة), I would be a man from Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

136
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:45,725
And if people take a road and the Ansaar(أنْصَار), take another road, I would follow the road of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار)

137
00:10:46,143 --> 00:10:48,428
O Allah, forgive, Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار),

138
00:10:48,452 --> 00:10:52,138
The sons of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار). And the grandsons of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

139
00:10:52,759 --> 00:10:58,271
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(ابوسعيد الخدري) say; They cried, they started crying, until their beards were wet

140
00:10:58,611 --> 00:11:02,848
and they said: We are pleased with Rasool Allah ﷺ as our share.

141
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:07,531
Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) are special, and Rasool Allah ﷺ told them that,

142
00:11:08,348 --> 00:11:10,117
you are different than the rest of the people.

143
00:11:10,464 --> 00:11:13,662
I'm giving the other people this money to bring them closer to Islam

144
00:11:13,686 --> 00:11:17,874
but I trust your Emaan(ايمان) and I trust your faith and I know that

145
00:11:18,066 --> 00:11:22,888
you are not in need of these worldly things to bring you closer to me and bring you closer to Allah,

146
00:11:23,404 --> 00:11:25,309
 you already have that in your hearts.

147
00:11:26,078 --> 00:11:29,396
The Ansaar(انصار), when they first met with Rasool Allah ﷺ

148
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:31,596
what was the deal between them and Rasool Allah ﷺ?

149
00:11:31,738 --> 00:11:37,216
We support you and we fight for you and what do we get in exchange of that?

150
00:11:37,412 --> 00:11:38,187
Al-Jannah(الجنة).

151
00:11:38,504 --> 00:11:41,822
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not promised them Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) from day one.

152
00:11:42,001 --> 00:11:44,730
The Ansaar(أنْصَار), we're in it, for the right reasons.

153
00:11:45,896 --> 00:11:53,572
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is reminding them with the blessings of Allah that came to Al-Ansaar(الأنصار),

154
00:11:53,683 --> 00:11:56,069
 when Rasool Allah ﷺ arrived in Madina.

155
00:11:56,737 --> 00:12:03,717
They were misguided, they were Kuffar(كفار), and what is a greatest disaster than being a Kafir(كافر)

156
00:12:04,687 --> 00:12:09,621
And they were guided through Muhammadﷺ, and what is the greater blessing than that

157
00:12:09,907 --> 00:12:10,587
nothing,

158
00:12:10,953 --> 00:12:15,169
 nothing counts when you compare it to the blessing of Hidayah(هداية).

159
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:17,309
And that's why brothers and sisters

160
00:12:17,485 --> 00:12:20,937
the most frequent Dua(دعا) that we make is Dua(دعا) we say in Fatiha(فاتحه),

161
00:12:20,961 --> 00:12:22,230
اِهْدِنَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ

162
00:12:22,254 --> 00:12:23,429
Guide us to the straight path.

163
00:12:24,113 --> 00:12:30,128
That is better for us than money, it's better than women, it's better than children.

164
00:12:30,168 --> 00:12:32,324
 It's better than having a house, it's better than everything.

165
00:12:32,911 --> 00:12:35,904
The best thing that you could have, better than having being healthy.

166
00:12:36,283 --> 00:12:40,216
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them: And you were poor and Allah enriched you.

167
00:12:40,470 --> 00:12:41,803
How did Allah enriched them?

168
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:48,476
I mean, in terms of the economy of Madina before it was based on agriculture

169
00:12:48,715 --> 00:12:57,097
and agriculture in Madina was actually going down because of the constant state of war that they were in,

170
00:12:57,335 --> 00:12:59,476
 because of the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

171
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:02,114
So, what does Rasool Allah ﷺ means enriched you through me?

172
00:13:02,422 --> 00:13:06,055
It means through the Ghanaem(غنائم) that are coming from Jihad(حهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

173
00:13:06,552 --> 00:13:08,555
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: And you were enemies

174
00:13:08,958 --> 00:13:13,905
Al-Aos(الأوس) and Khazraj(خزرج) were at the throats of each other, and Allah has brought them together.

175
00:13:14,647 --> 00:13:17,994
So, they agreed and they said: All favors belong to Allah and His Messenger.

176
00:13:18,018 --> 00:13:20,510
We can't reject that and we can't complain!

177
00:13:21,178 --> 00:13:23,019
But then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

178
00:13:23,297 --> 00:13:32,489
On the other hand, you could also, tell me, that I was rejected by my people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

179
00:13:33,188 --> 00:13:35,981
And it is, we who believe.

180
00:13:36,511 --> 00:13:41,309
You can say that you were betrayed by your people and we are the ones, who supported you.

181
00:13:41,813 --> 00:13:45,278
You can say that you were a refugitive and you had nowhere to go.

182
00:13:45,757 --> 00:13:48,034
And there was a bounty on you.

183
00:13:48,263 --> 00:13:52,891
And it is we, who provided you with the home and a base to spread the Da'wah(دعوة) from.

184
00:13:53,226 --> 00:14:00,453
And you could also say that Rasool Allah ﷺ was poor and he had nothing and we are the ones, who hosted him.

185
00:14:01,250 --> 00:14:04,624
But the Ansaar(أنْصَار) obviously would not say that, they would not complain,

186
00:14:05,237 --> 00:14:07,314
they would not brag about, what they have done.

187
00:14:07,873 --> 00:14:10,970
Because they consider everything to be a blessing from Allahعَزّوجَلّ

188
00:14:11,482 --> 00:14:15,948
and everything good that they did, they considered it to be from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

189
00:14:16,483 --> 00:14:20,093
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling them that, this is a small material gain.

190
00:14:20,117 --> 00:14:21,641
لُعَاعَةٍ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا

191
00:14:22,311 --> 00:14:26,000
And I'm giving it to these people not because I love them, not because I like them.

192
00:14:26,024 --> 00:14:28,696
It is because I want to bring them closer to Islam.

193
00:14:28,736 --> 00:14:29,555
 أَتَألَّفْهُمْ

194
00:14:29,716 --> 00:14:30,284
These are called;

195
00:14:30,324 --> 00:14:31,562
مُؤلَّفُة قُلُوْبُهُمْ

196
00:14:32,442 --> 00:14:34,404
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them something,

197
00:14:34,821 --> 00:14:40,476
which only people who understand the greatness of Rasool Allah ﷺ

198
00:14:41,132 --> 00:14:45,962
he told them that people are going back with sheep and camels,

199
00:14:46,904 --> 00:14:49,419
while you are going back to your homes with Rasool Ullah.

200
00:14:50,332 --> 00:14:54,518
I am going back with you, I'm not going to stay in Makkah, I'm going back with you.

201
00:14:55,327 --> 00:14:58,251
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling them that if it wasn't for Hijrah(هجرة),

202
00:14:58,275 --> 00:15:00,487
because Rasool Allah ﷺ is counted as a Muhajir(مهاجر)

203
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:03,330
which is a greater status then Ansaari(انصاري).

204
00:15:03,544 --> 00:15:05,957
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says; If it wasn't for Hijrah(هجرة).

205
00:15:06,242 --> 00:15:09,105
I would count myself as a member of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار)

206
00:15:09,648 --> 00:15:14,526
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling them, if all the people take a certain road,

207
00:15:14,758 --> 00:15:18,698
while you take another road, I would follow yours, I would be with you.

208
00:15:19,488 --> 00:15:23,570
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ made this lovely Dua(دعا) for Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار);

209
00:15:23,965 --> 00:15:27,499
O Allah forgive the Ansaar(انصار), Forgive the sons of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار),

210
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:30,823
And forgive the grandsons of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار)!

211
00:15:31,199 --> 00:15:37,313
And this, when the Ansaar رضي الله عنهم heard these words they cried, until their beards were wet.

212
00:15:37,911 --> 00:15:42,138
And they said: We are pleased with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

213
00:15:43,642 --> 00:15:46,997
There are different narrations as I mentioned in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم)

214
00:15:48,087 --> 00:15:51,264
in one of them there was a statement that caught my attention.

215
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:53,042
Hishaam(هشام) says;

216
00:15:53,219 --> 00:15:57,631
قُلْتِ يَا اَبَا حَمْزَه وَاَنْتَ شَاهِدْ ذَالِكْ، قَالَ: اَنَس أغيب عنه

217
00:15:58,323 --> 00:16:04,870
Hishaam(هشام), who's the Tabie(تابعي) narrating the Hadith(حديث) is asking; Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك), whose Kuniya(كنيه) is Abu Hamza(أبوحمزه).

218
00:16:04,910 --> 00:16:08,665
 He's saying; O Abu Hamza(أبو حمزه) and you have witness that

219
00:16:09,216 --> 00:16:11,904
Anas(انس) said: And where else would I be?

220
00:16:12,377 --> 00:16:16,420
What caught my attention, here is the response that Anas(انس) gave.

221
00:16:16,823 --> 00:16:18,188
He didn't say: Yes, I was there.

222
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:20,140
He told him: And where else would I be?

223
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:27,350
And this shows us, a virtue of Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه being the servant of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

224
00:16:27,374 --> 00:16:31,886
He was always with Rasool Allah ﷺ and such an event would not miss him.

225
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:33,930
He would definitely, be there.

226
00:16:34,733 --> 00:16:42,267
And that's why it's mentioned that Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) used to have so many dreams of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

227
00:16:42,582 --> 00:16:47,108
That it goes to the extent that they mentioned that he used to dream about Rasool Allah ﷺ every night.

228
00:16:47,505 --> 00:16:49,459
As he was always with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

229
00:16:50,029 --> 00:16:54,627
An Zohri(عن أظهري), Rasool Allah gave Al-Akrah Bin Habis(اقراء بن حابس) One hundred(100) camels

230
00:16:54,651 --> 00:16:57,875
and he gave Uyeyna Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن) One hundred(100) camels.

231
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:02,224
But he gave Abbas Bin Mardaas(عباس بن مرداس), who was also a chief of the tribe only 50.

232
00:17:02,681 --> 00:17:09,716
So, Al-Abbas(العباس) made some lines of poetry talking about this and saying that

233
00:17:10,161 --> 00:17:15,982
how can my share be less than the share of Al-Akrah Bin Habis(اقرع بن حابس) and Uyeynah(عيينه)

234
00:17:16,275 --> 00:17:21,112
when my father and their fathers were on an equal footing.

235
00:17:21,780 --> 00:17:29,454
And Az-Zuhri(ألظهري) mentions, this narration, he says, that these words reached to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

236
00:17:29,478 --> 00:17:30,183
So Rasool Allah said;

237
00:17:30,223 --> 00:17:36,476
 اَنْتَ الْقَائِلْ فاصْبَح نَهْبِيْ وَنَهْبُي الْعَبِيْدِ بَيْنَ الْاَقْرَعْ وَعُيَيْنَهْ

238
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:39,198
فقالَ: ابو بكر مَا هَكذا قال: يا رسول الله

239
00:17:39,447 --> 00:17:44,511
وَلَكِنْ وَلله مَاكُنْتَ بِشَاعِرٍ وَمَا يَنْبَغِيْ لَكْ فقال: كَيْفَ قَال

240
00:17:44,592 --> 00:17:51,179
فَانْشَدَه’ ابو بكر، فقالَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم هُمَا سَوَاءْ مَا يَضُرُّكَ بَأيِّهِمَا بَدَاتْ، َ

241
00:17:51,511 --> 00:17:55,909
ثُمَّ قَالَ رسول الله صلوات الله ولسلام عليه اِقْطَعُوْ عَنِّيْ لِسَانه

242
00:17:56,658 --> 00:18:03,093
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Are you the one, who says and then Rasool Ullah mentioned one line of this poem,

243
00:18:03,283 --> 00:18:08,973
 that my share and the share of my horse is less than the share of Al-Akrah(اقرع) and Uyeynah(عيينه).

244
00:18:09,096 --> 00:18:12,372
While in the poem Uyeynah(عيينه) is mentioned before Akrah(اقرع).

245
00:18:12,396 --> 00:18:14,353
Rasool Allah mentioned Al-Akrah(اقرع) before Uyeynah(عيينه).

246
00:18:14,377 --> 00:18:17,627
So, Rasool Ullah did not mention the line of poetry correctly.

247
00:18:17,651 --> 00:18:21,978
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) told Rasool Allah ﷺ that is not how he said it

248
00:18:22,732 --> 00:18:28,304
but In the name of Allah, you are not a poet and it's not appropriate for you to be one

249
00:18:28,598 --> 00:18:30,537
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What did he say?

250
00:18:30,759 --> 00:18:33,184
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) mentioned the line as it should be.

251
00:18:33,223 --> 00:18:38,293
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: They are equal, it doesn't matter which one is mentioned first.

252
00:18:38,673 --> 00:18:44,326
And the reason why I'm bringing up this narration, is to show you that Rasool Allah ﷺ was not a poet

253
00:18:45,072 --> 00:18:54,873
and even when he came to recite that line, he did not follow the meter of the poetry as was known in those times

254
00:18:55,316 --> 00:19:01,330
 because Allahعَزّوجَلّ has kept Rasool Allah ﷺ away from poetry,

255
00:19:01,719 --> 00:19:05,258
but Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) mentioned that to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said that

256
00:19:05,746 --> 00:19:08,967
it is not Al-Akrah(الاقرع) before Uyeynah(عيينه) but Uyeynah(عيينه) should be before Akrah(الاقرع).

257
00:19:08,991 --> 00:19:14,817
Anyway the man said: Yes! So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Cut away his tongue.

258
00:19:15,311 --> 00:19:21,232
Some people thought that Rasool Allah ﷺ literally meant that, the tongue of Al-Abbas(العباس) should be cut.

259
00:19:21,385 --> 00:19:26,113
When Rasool Allah ﷺ meant that you should give him another 50

260
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:31,243
and that would cut away his tongue, figuratively speaking,

261
00:19:31,283 --> 00:19:34,681
 he will not go around mentioning these words anymore.

262
00:19:35,058 --> 00:19:38,833
And he was given a 100 just like Al-Akrah(الاقرع) and Uyeynah(عيينه).

263
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:46,132
To show you what Rasool Allah ﷺ them was doing the reason, justification behind it.

264
00:19:46,933 --> 00:19:51,394
In an authentic narration from Safwaan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان إبن أمية), he said;

265
00:19:51,816 --> 00:19:58,561
مَا زالَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يُعْطِيْنِيْ مِنْ غَنَائِمِ حُنَيْنِ وَهُوَ اَبْغَضُ خَلْقِ اِلَيَّ

266
00:19:58,901 --> 00:20:01,875
حَتَّى مَا خَلَقَ اللهُ شَيْئا اَحَبَّ اِلَيَّ مِنْهُ

267
00:20:02,161 --> 00:20:07,445
Safwaan(صفوان) says: Rasool Allah ﷺ kept on giving me from the booty of Hunain(حنين)

268
00:20:07,973 --> 00:20:11,394
and he was the worst of the creation to me,

269
00:20:11,678 --> 00:20:17,550
until Allah has not created anything that was more beloved to me than him.

270
00:20:18,175 --> 00:20:23,842
So, it was these gifts that Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving them that soften their hearts

271
00:20:23,866 --> 00:20:26,224
and made them love Rasool Allah ﷺ.

272
00:20:26,248 --> 00:20:30,843
Really brothers and sisters, when you look at the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, you see

273
00:20:31,254 --> 00:20:35,184
that Rasool Allah ﷺ was a master in dealing with people.

274
00:20:35,764 --> 00:20:46,998
Rasool Allah ﷺ was blessed by Allah with the ability of drawing together the hearts of the community

275
00:20:47,409 --> 00:20:51,447
and forging together an Ummah(امة) and Allahعَزّوجَلّ told him.

276
00:20:51,873 --> 00:21:05,746
لَوْ أَنْفَقْتَ مَا فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا مَا أَلَّفْتَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِهِمْ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ أَلَّفَ بَيْنَهُمْ ۚ

277
00:21:05,836 --> 00:21:11,413
If you would spend all of that which is in the world to bring together their hearts you would not do so.

278
00:21:11,492 --> 00:21:13,344
 But it is Allah who brought them together.

279
00:21:13,505 --> 00:21:16,222
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has brought these people together.

280
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:21,936
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the means for bringing them together.

281
00:21:21,968 --> 00:21:27,079
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling Muhammadﷺ, that it is not you but it is from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

282
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:32,655
But the point here to make is that Rasool Allah ﷺ we need to understand and learn his Sunnah(سنة).

283
00:21:33,855 --> 00:21:37,827
You know, we sometimes have a limited understanding of what Sunnah(سنة) is.

284
00:21:38,542 --> 00:21:41,113
The way Rasool Allah ﷺ dealt with people, is Sunnah(سنة).

285
00:21:41,915 --> 00:21:43,874
The way he made Da'wah(دعوة) is Sunnah(سنة)

286
00:21:44,366 --> 00:21:48,421
The way Rasool Allah ﷺ fought is Sunnah(سنة), these are all parts of Sunnah(سنة).

287
00:21:48,831 --> 00:21:56,385
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving Safwaan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان إبن أمية), who was an enemy of Rasool Ullah until that moment,

288
00:21:56,854 --> 00:22:00,825
Rasool Allah ﷺ put all of that aside, put it behind him

289
00:22:01,407 --> 00:22:06,522
and was giving Safwaan(صفوان) until, Safwaan(صفوان) was pleased and happy

290
00:22:06,546 --> 00:22:12,773
and he says and admits that, Muhammadﷺ was the most disliked person to me

291
00:22:13,418 --> 00:22:16,071
and now I love him more than anybody else.

292
00:22:17,091 --> 00:22:18,513
Bukhari(إلبخاري) narrates;

293
00:22:18,613 --> 00:22:28,377
 حدثنا عمرو بن تغلِب: أَنَّ رسول الله ﷺ أُتِيَّ بِمَالٍ أَوْ سَبِّيٍ فَقَسَّمَه’ فَأعْطَى رِجَالًا، وَتَرَكَ رِجَالًا

294
00:22:28,702 --> 00:22:35,384
فَبَلَغَه’ أَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَرَكَهُمْ عَتَبُوْا، فَحَمِدَ الله، وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ قَالْ: أَمَّا بَعْدَ:

295
00:22:35,553 --> 00:22:42,553
فَوَالله إِنِّيْ لِأُعْطِي الرَّجُلَ، وَأَدَعُ الرَّجُلْ، وَالَّذِيْ أَدَعُ أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ مِنَّ الَّذِيْ أُعْطِيْ

296
00:22:43,042 --> 00:22:47,596
وَلَكِنِّي إِنَّمَا أُعْطِيْ أَقْوَاماً لِمَا أَرَى فِيْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مِنَّ الْجَزَعْ وَالْهَلَعْ،

297
00:22:47,834 --> 00:22:51,885
 وَأكِلُ أَقْوَاماً إِلَى مَا جَعَلَ الله فِيْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مِنَّ الْغِنَى وَالْخَيْر

298
00:22:52,097 --> 00:22:56,337
فيهُمْ عمرو بن تغلب، فَوَالله عمرو يقول

299
00:22:56,362 --> 00:23:01,923
فَوَالله مَا أُحِبُّ أَنَّ لِيْ بِكَلِمَةِ رسول الله ﷺ حُمْرً النَّعْمْ

300
00:23:02,689 --> 00:23:09,369
Amr Bin Taghlib(عمرو بن تغلب) says; That Rasool Allah ﷺ was distributing money or Sabbi(سبي),

301
00:23:09,409 --> 00:23:10,920
 Sabbi(سبي) are the women and children.

302
00:23:11,211 --> 00:23:14,580
So, he distributed it, so he gave some men and he left others.

303
00:23:15,127 --> 00:23:20,054
So, Rasool Ullah was told that the ones whom he left were upset that they were left out.

304
00:23:20,339 --> 00:23:23,643
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ praised Allah and thanked Him and then said;

305
00:23:23,874 --> 00:23:29,766
 In the name of Allah I would give a man and I would leave out another man.

306
00:23:30,035 --> 00:23:34,646
And the one I leave out is more beloved to me than the one I give.

307
00:23:34,892 --> 00:23:39,327
But I am giving people because I see greed in their hearts.

308
00:23:39,858 --> 00:23:47,335
And I entrust others to what Allah has blessed them with contentment and good in their hearts.

309
00:23:47,570 --> 00:23:49,389
And one of them is Amr Bin Taghlib(عمرو بن تغلب).

310
00:23:49,682 --> 00:23:58,298
Amr Bin Taghlib(عمرو بن تغلب) then says; In the name of Allah, I love these words of Rasool Allah ﷺ more than all of the red camels.

311
00:23:58,322 --> 00:24:02,522
And the red camels we mentioned before are the most valuable type of camels.

312
00:24:02,547 --> 00:24:05,772
I mean, if you would give me the entire world of red camels,

313
00:24:06,151 --> 00:24:11,538
I would leave that and rather have Rasool Allah ﷺ give me this badge of honor.

314
00:24:12,280 --> 00:24:16,123
So, you see how Rasool Allah ﷺ has given Safwaan(صفوان)

315
00:24:16,446 --> 00:24:18,820
and that made Safwaan(صفوان) love Rasool Allah ﷺ

316
00:24:19,174 --> 00:24:22,074
and Rasool Ullah prevented Amr Bin Taghlib(عمرو بن تغلب)

317
00:24:22,285 --> 00:24:25,367
and that made Amr Bin Taghlib(عمرو بن تغلب) love Rasool Allah ﷺ more

318
00:24:25,558 --> 00:24:29,485
because Rasool Allah ﷺ mentioned his name and said, that I entrust him to his Eeman(إيمان).

319
00:24:30,057 --> 00:24:36,233
But there were some people, who not only were greedy, but they were complaining

320
00:24:36,526 --> 00:24:41,886
and we will see an example of that and this is mentioned in Bukhari(بخاريْ)

321
00:24:42,140 --> 00:24:44,055
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(ابوسعيد الخدري) narrates;

322
00:24:44,079 --> 00:24:53,672
قالَ: بَيْنَمَا نَحْنُ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ يَقْسِمُ قِسْمًا ، أَتَاهُ ذُو الخُوَيْصِرَةِوَهُوَ رَجُلٌ مِنْ بَنِي تَمِيمٍ ،

323
00:24:54,378 --> 00:24:56,283
 فَقَالَ : يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ اِعْدِلْ ،

324
00:24:56,648 --> 00:24:59,291
فَقَالَ : وَيْلَكَ ، وَمَنْ يَعْدِلُ إِذَا لَمْ أَعْدِلْ

325
00:24:59,501 --> 00:25:02,739
قَدْ خِبْتَ وَخَسِرْتَ إِنْ لَمْ أَكُنْ أَعْدِلُ

326
00:25:03,435 --> 00:25:08,602
فَقَالَ عُمَرُ : يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ، اِئْذَنْ لِي فِيهِ فَأَضْرِبَ عُنُقَهُ ؟

327
00:25:08,904 --> 00:25:14,313
فَقَالَ : دَعْهُ ، فَإِنَّ لَهُ أَصْحَابًا يَحْقِرُ أَحَدُكُمْ صَلاَتَهُ مَعَ صَلاَتِهِمْ ،

328
00:25:14,432 --> 00:25:19,376
وَصِيَامَهُ مَعَ صِيَامِهِمْ ، يَقْرَءُونَ القُرْآنَ لاَ يُجَاوِزُ تَرَاقِيَهُمْ

329
00:25:19,537 --> 00:25:25,846
يَمْرُقُونَ مِنَ الدِّينِ كَمَا يَمْرُقُ السَّهْمُ مِنَ الرَّمِيَّةِ ، يُنْظَرُ إِلَى نَصْلِهِ فَلاَ يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ

330
00:25:25,870 --> 00:25:34,981
ثُمَّ يُنْظَرُ إِلَى رِصَافِهِ فَمَا يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ ، ثُمَّ يُنْظَرُ إِلَى نَضِيِّهِ ، - وَهُوَ قِدْحُهُ - ، فَلاَ يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ

331
00:25:35,368 --> 00:25:38,543
ثُمَّ يُنْظَرُ إِلَى قُذَذِهِ فَلاَ يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ ،

332
00:25:38,654 --> 00:25:46,118
قَدْ سَبَقَ الفَرْثَ وَالدَّمَ ، آيَتُهُمْ رَجُلٌ أَسْوَدُ ، إِحْدَى عَضُدَيْهِ مِثْلُ ثَدْيِ المَرْأَةِ

333
00:25:46,182 --> 00:25:51,541
أَوْ مِثْلُ البَضْعَةِ تَدَرْدَرُ ، وَيَخْرُجُونَ عَلَى حِينِ فُرْقَةٍ مِنَ النَّاسِ

334
00:25:51,702 --> 00:25:57,169
قَالَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ : فَأَشْهَدُ أَنِّي سَمِعْتُ هَذَا الحَدِيثَ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ

335
00:25:57,478 --> 00:26:01,465
وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ عَلِيَّ بْنَ أَبِي طَالِبٍ قَاتَلَهُمْ وَأَنَا مَعَهُ

336
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:08,923
فَأَمَرَ بِذَلِكَ الرَّجُلِ فَالْتُمِسَ فَأُتِيَ بِهِ ، حَتَّى نَظَرْتُ إِلَيْهِ عَلَى نَعْتِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الَّذِي نَعَتَهُ

337
00:26:09,290 --> 00:26:13,978
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(ابو سعيد الخدري) says; We were with Rasool Allah ﷺ while he was distributing a booty

338
00:26:14,412 --> 00:26:17,971
and he was approached by Zul Khuwaisrah(ذو الخويسره) and he is a man from Bannu Tamim(بنو تميم).

339
00:26:18,562 --> 00:26:21,095
So, he said: O Rasool Ullah, be just.

340
00:26:21,642 --> 00:26:25,781
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), I mean, this man is speaking to Rasool Allah ﷺ

341
00:26:26,279 --> 00:26:30,161
the messenger from Allah, and he's telling him: Be just.

342
00:26:30,376 --> 00:26:37,625
This man, who was until, quite a short while ago, a disbeliever making Sujood(سجود) to an idol

343
00:26:37,738 --> 00:26:41,014
is telling the best of creation, Be just.

344
00:26:41,425 --> 00:26:46,802
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Woe to you and who would be just if I am not just.

345
00:26:47,728 --> 00:26:52,892
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said: O Rasool Ullah allow me, to cut off his neck.

346
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:57,394
Rasool Allah ﷺ said leave him because he will have companions

347
00:26:57,766 --> 00:27:00,691
you will belittle your Salah(صلاة) to their Salah(صلاة)

348
00:27:01,062 --> 00:27:04,185
and you would belittle your fasting, compared to their fasting

349
00:27:04,524 --> 00:27:07,830
they would recite Qur'an but it would not leave their throats.

350
00:27:08,084 --> 00:27:10,025
It would not go beyond their throats

351
00:27:10,598 --> 00:27:15,706
they would leave the religion, just like an arrow would leave its target.

352
00:27:16,265 --> 00:27:21,545
So, you would look at the blade, and there's no blood on it.

353
00:27:21,878 --> 00:27:26,425
And then you would look at the binding, and you would not find nothing on it.

354
00:27:26,632 --> 00:27:29,532
And you would look at the rest of the arrow,

355
00:27:29,556 --> 00:27:33,237
and you would find the shaft and you would find nothing on it.

356
00:27:33,740 --> 00:27:35,780
An explanation of what this is.?

357
00:27:36,018 --> 00:27:41,320
 If an archer is strong and he shoots the arrow with such force,

358
00:27:41,529 --> 00:27:45,861
the arrow could hit the game and could pass to it so fast

359
00:27:46,250 --> 00:27:52,618
that the archer cannot even recognize, that the target was hit.

360
00:27:53,021 --> 00:27:57,748
And then he goes to pick up the arrow, to see if there's any traces of blood on it.

361
00:27:58,541 --> 00:28:00,861
And he would find nothing, he would look at the blade, there's nothing

362
00:28:00,885 --> 00:28:05,428
he would look at the binding that brings the blade to the shaft, he would find nothing

363
00:28:05,452 --> 00:28:08,968
then he would look at the shaft itself and he would find nothing.

364
00:28:09,714 --> 00:28:15,069
This is an analogy that Rasool Allah ﷺ gave of how fast these people would leave religion.

365
00:28:15,094 --> 00:28:23,169
I mean, they are so extreme that they would leave the religion so swiftly, you couldn't even recognize that.

366
00:28:24,299 --> 00:28:28,686
And this is a very interesting analogy that Rasool Allah ﷺ gave about these people.

367
00:28:29,389 --> 00:28:35,189
Because they pray and Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that they're praying more than the Sahabah(صحابه)

368
00:28:35,670 --> 00:28:38,467
and they are fasting and they're fasting more

369
00:28:38,815 --> 00:28:41,774
and they recite Qur'an, but it doesn't leave their throats.

370
00:28:41,798 --> 00:28:44,253
Why? Because they're not following the meanings.

371
00:28:44,277 --> 00:28:48,068
It's just voice coming out from the throat but there's no implication of it.

372
00:28:48,619 --> 00:28:52,723
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said, and their sign is a dark man

373
00:28:52,868 --> 00:28:58,601
and one of his arms I mean, he doesn't have a full arm he just has a trunk of an arm

374
00:28:58,833 --> 00:29:01,556
and it looks like a breast of a woman.

375
00:29:02,279 --> 00:29:07,531
So, Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(ابوسعيد الخدري) said: I testified that I heard these words from Rasool Allah ﷺ

376
00:29:07,747 --> 00:29:11,429
and I testify that Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is the one, who fought them

377
00:29:11,469 --> 00:29:16,622
and I was with him and he ordered that you search for that man and we found him

378
00:29:16,970 --> 00:29:22,627
and we saw that the description of Rasool Allah ﷺ, this man fitted exactly.

379
00:29:22,990 --> 00:29:28,904
Let's see some words from Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر), in his commentary on this Hadith(حديث);

380
00:29:29,080 --> 00:29:30,088
قَالَ اِبْنِ هُبَيْرَهْ

381
00:29:30,264 --> 00:29:32,272
Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر) says, that Ibn Hubairah(ابن هبيره) said;

382
00:29:32,620 --> 00:29:37,116
وَفِي الْحَدِيثِ أَنَّ قِتَالَ الْخَوَارِجِ أَوْلَى مِنْ قِتَالِ الْمُشْرِكِينَ

383
00:29:37,277 --> 00:29:42,353
وَالْحِكْمَةُ فِيهِ أَنَّ فِي قِتَالِهِمْ حِفْظَ رَأْسِ مَالِ الْإِسْلَامِ

384
00:29:42,724 --> 00:29:47,314
وَفِي قِتَالِ أَهْلِ الشِّرْكِ طَلَبُ الرِّبْحِ، وَحِفْظُ رَأْسِ الْمَالِ أَوْلَى

385
00:29:47,896 --> 00:29:55,574
In this Hadith(حديث), we learn that fighting the Khawarij(خوارج) is a priority over fighting the disbelievers.

386
00:29:56,125 --> 00:30:01,622
And the wisdom behind that, is because fighting the KhawariJ(خوارج) is a protection of the capital,

387
00:30:01,970 --> 00:30:05,228
while fighting the disbelievers is seeking profit

388
00:30:05,654 --> 00:30:10,297
and protecting the capital takes precedence, over making a profit.

389
00:30:10,321 --> 00:30:14,093
And this is a rule that applies to fighting all of the Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

390
00:30:14,355 --> 00:30:18,230
Because they are eating the Ummah(امة) from within.

391
00:30:18,461 --> 00:30:20,243
While when you fight the disbelievers

392
00:30:20,472 --> 00:30:26,779
you're fighting them to bring them obviously here, they're talking about fighting the disbelievers in terms of Da'wah(دعوة).

393
00:30:26,944 --> 00:30:31,087
So, protecting the capital takes precedence over making profit.

394
00:30:31,502 --> 00:30:32,442
And then he says;

395
00:30:32,704 --> 00:30:39,754
وَفِيْهِ الْتَحْذِيْرمِنَّ الْغُلُوِّفِيْ الدِّيَانَه وَالتَنَطَّعْ فِي الْعِبَادَهْ بِالْحَمْلِ عَلَى النَفْسِ فِيْمَا لَمْ يَاْذَنْ فِيْهِ الشَّرْعَ

396
00:30:40,078 --> 00:30:44,748
And he said: There's a warning in this Hadith(حديث) from going to extremes, in religion

397
00:30:45,331 --> 00:30:52,212
and going to extremes in worship in ways that Islam has not allowed, Shariyah(شريعة) has not allowed.

398
00:30:53,061 --> 00:30:53,631
And then he says;

399
00:30:53,673 --> 00:31:02,182
وَاِنَّمَا نَدَبَ اِلَى شِّدَةِ عَلَى الْكُفَّارِ وَاِلَى رَاْفَةِ بِالْمُؤمِنِيْنَ فَعَكَسَ ذَالِكَ الْخَوَارِجْ كَمَا تَقَدَّمَ بَيَانَهْ

400
00:31:02,843 --> 00:31:09,950
Our religion has encouraged us to be rough with the Kuffar(كفار) and soft with the believers.

401
00:31:10,037 --> 00:31:13,407
And the Khawarij(الخوارج) did the opposite of that, like we have seen

402
00:31:13,888 --> 00:31:19,253
because Rasool Allah ﷺ gives us a very important sign of the signs of Al-Khawarij(الخوارج)

403
00:31:19,293 --> 00:31:23,911
 and it's very important to keep in mind whenever we want to know who the Khawarij(خوارج) are?

404
00:31:24,189 --> 00:31:25,549
And that sign is;

405
00:31:25,676 --> 00:31:28,962
يَقْتُلُوْنَ اَهْلَ الْاِسْلَامِ وَيَتْرَكُوْنَ اَهْلَ الْاَوْسَانْ

406
00:31:29,099 --> 00:31:32,247
They kill the Muslims and they leave the disbelievers.

407
00:31:32,271 --> 00:31:34,891
This is an important sign of the signs of the Khawarij(خوارج).

408
00:31:35,020 --> 00:31:41,459
An example of that Abdallah Bin Khabbab(عبدالله بن خباب), he is the son of the companion Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت),

409
00:31:41,916 --> 00:31:47,394
he was traveling along with his wife and he was stopped by the Khawarij(خوارج).

410
00:31:47,648 --> 00:31:50,865
They said: Who are you.? He said: I am the son of Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت).

411
00:31:50,986 --> 00:31:53,764
Everybody knows who he is, a companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

412
00:31:54,082 --> 00:31:55,602
And they killed him

413
00:31:55,865 --> 00:31:59,693
and they opened up the stomach of his wife

414
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:04,411
and killed her and drew out the fetus, she was pregnant.

415
00:32:05,353 --> 00:32:10,959
And then, they took some belongings that were owned by Christian or a Jew.

416
00:32:11,260 --> 00:32:15,120
And then some of them said: No, you have to return it, because these are Ahluz-Zimmah(أهل ضمه).

417
00:32:15,390 --> 00:32:16,882
So, you can see an example here.

418
00:32:17,205 --> 00:32:19,978
They are following Warra'a(ورع) and Taqwa(تقوى) when it comes to Ahluz-Zimmah(أهل ضمه)

419
00:32:20,003 --> 00:32:26,517
but when it comes to the Muslims, they killed the son of a companion of Rasool Allah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

420
00:32:26,897 --> 00:32:30,771
This is one of the most important qualities of Khawarij(خوارج)

421
00:32:31,041 --> 00:32:34,400
is their animosity, hatred, roughness toward Muslims.

422
00:32:34,708 --> 00:32:38,153
And then when it comes to the Kuffar(كفار), they turned a blind eye towards them.

423
00:32:38,868 --> 00:32:39,639
وَفِيْهِ جَوَازُ

424
00:32:39,663 --> 00:32:45,917
And by the way, that incident that I mentioned was, started the war between Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and Khawarij(خوارج).

425
00:32:45,972 --> 00:32:52,464
Because Ali(على) said: Leave them alone until, they kill or they rob, then we will fight them.

426
00:32:52,836 --> 00:32:55,963
So, when they killed Abdallah Bin Khabbab(عبدالله بن خباب) and they took his belongings

427
00:32:55,987 --> 00:32:59,258
that is when Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) ordered that, they should be fought.

428
00:32:59,729 --> 00:33:00,537
And then he says;

429
00:33:01,221 --> 00:33:09,726
وَفِيْهِ جَوَازُ قِتَالِ مَنْ خَرَجَ عَنْ طَاعَةِ الْاِمَامُ الْعَادِلْ ، وَمَنْ نَصَبَ الْحَرْبَ فَقَاتَلَ عَلَى اَعْتَقَادٍ فَاسِدْ

430
00:33:10,059 --> 00:33:19,418
He says; There is evidence here for fighting, the ones who revolt against the just Imam(إمام), the just leader

431
00:33:20,175 --> 00:33:24,215
and the ones, who are fighting for a false belief.

432
00:33:24,805 --> 00:33:30,104
So, there is an evidence here for fighting the ones, who are fighting for a false belief,

433
00:33:30,135 --> 00:33:33,548
and fighting the ones, who revolt against a just leader

434
00:33:33,683 --> 00:33:37,120
such as Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), the ones who revolt against him.

435
00:33:37,952 --> 00:33:42,934
وَمَنْ خَرَجَ يَقْطَعَ الطُّرُقْ وَيُخِيْفِ السَّبِيْلَ وَيَسْعَى فِيْ الْاَرْضِ بِالْفَسَادْ

436
00:33:43,087 --> 00:33:48,640
And the ones, who spread corruption on earth and commit armed robbery

437
00:33:48,793 --> 00:33:51,185
there is an evidence here that they should be fought.

438
00:33:51,493 --> 00:33:54,683
And keep note of what Ibn Hajar(ابن حجر) is saying next.

439
00:33:55,031 --> 00:34:06,074
وَاَمَّا مَنْ خَرَجَ عَنْ طَاعَةِ اِمَامٍ جَاِئٍر اَرَادَ الْغَلَبَةَ عَلَى مَالِهِ اَوْ نَفْسِهِ اَوْ اَهْلِهِ فَهُوَ مَعْذُوْرٌ وَلَايَحِلُّ قِتَالُهْ

440
00:34:06,602 --> 00:34:12,915
He says; But the ones revolt against an oppressive leader.

441
00:34:13,403 --> 00:34:17,085
And notice here, he is not saying that disbelieving leader, he is saying an oppressive leader.

442
00:34:17,870 --> 00:34:26,096
Who wants to take over his wealth, or to kill him, or to abuse his family, then he is excused.

443
00:34:26,121 --> 00:34:27,909
And it is not allowed to fight him.

444
00:34:28,304 --> 00:34:31,506
So, the ones who revolt against the unjust leaders.

445
00:34:31,530 --> 00:34:34,228
Ibn Hajar(ابن حجر) is saying that it is Haram(حرام) to fight them

446
00:34:34,795 --> 00:34:36,921
and they are excused for fighting.

447
00:34:37,855 --> 00:34:46,965
And he says that if the police force or the army of an unjust ruler comes to take away your wealth or to kill you

448
00:34:47,291 --> 00:34:50,806
 or to abuse your family then you can fight back.

449
00:34:50,831 --> 00:34:51,153
He says;

450
00:34:51,193 --> 00:34:55,408
 وَلَايَحِلُّ قِتَالُهْ وَلَه’ اَنْ يَدْفَعَ عَنْ نَفْسِهِ وَمَالِهِ وَاَهْلِهِ بِقَدَرْ طَاقَتِهْ

451
00:34:55,758 --> 00:35:00,739
And you can defend yourself and your wealth and your family according to your ability.

452
00:35:00,899 --> 00:35:03,029
So, and this is talking about the unjust leader.

453
00:35:03,415 --> 00:35:08,185
But if the leader is a disbeliever then it is the consensus of the Ulemaa(علماء) that it is Wajib(واجب),

454
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:15,476
it is obligatory to fight him, you cannot submit to a disbelieving leader.

455
00:35:16,343 --> 00:35:18,272
وَسَيَاتِيْ بِيَانُ ذَالِكَ فِيْ كِتَابِ الْفِتَنْ

456
00:35:18,296 --> 00:35:22,544
He said: And we will explain that in the book of Fittan(فتن).

457
00:35:22,687 --> 00:35:23,472
And then he says;

458
00:35:23,698 --> 00:35:28,532
 وَقَدْ اَخْرَجَ الطَّبَرِيْ بِسَنَدٍ صَحِيْح عَنْ عبد الله بن حارث

459
00:35:28,942 --> 00:35:33,764
عَنْ رَجُلٍ مِنْ بَنِيْ نَضَرْ عَنْ عَلِي وَذَكَرَ الْخَوَارج فَقَال

460
00:35:34,018 --> 00:35:41,991
اِنْ خَالَفُوْا اِمَامًا عَدْلًا فَقَاتِلُوْهُمْ، وَاِنْ خَالَفُوْا اِمَامًا جَاِئرًا فَلَا تُقَاتِلُوْهُمْ فَاِنَّ لَهُمْ مَقَالًا

461
00:35:42,760 --> 00:35:47,332
At-Tabari(الطبري) narrates with an authentic chain from Abdullah Bin Harith(عَبد الله بن حارث),

462
00:35:47,758 --> 00:35:51,527
from a man from Banni Nazar(بني نضر) from Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

463
00:35:51,695 --> 00:35:54,050
that he said about Al-Khawarij(الخوارج),

464
00:35:54,193 --> 00:35:59,878
if they go against a just ruler then they should be fought.

465
00:36:00,226 --> 00:36:07,467
But if they go against an unjust ruler, then do not fight them because they have an evidence.

466
00:36:07,993 --> 00:36:16,079
قُلْت :وَعَلَى ذَالِكْ يُحْمَلْ مَا وَقَعَ لاْحُسَيْن بِن عَلي ثٌمَّ لِاَهْلِ الْمَدِيْنَه فِيْ الْحَرَّةْ

467
00:36:16,185 --> 00:36:24,556
ثُمَّ لِعَبْدِالله بِن زُبَيْر ثُمَّ لِلْقُرَّاءِ الَّذِيْنَ خَرَجُوْاعَلَى الْحُجَاجْ فِيْ قِصَّةِ عبد الرحمن بن محمدبن اَلْاَشْعَثْ وَالله اَعْلَمْ

468
00:36:24,898 --> 00:36:30,969
And then he says, and that is what we should consider, happend with Al-Hussain Bin Ali(ألحسين بن علي)

469
00:36:31,184 --> 00:36:33,654
and people of Madina when they revolted.

470
00:36:33,956 --> 00:36:39,866
And Abdallah Bin Zubair(عبد الله بن زبير) and then the scholars who revolted against Al-Hujjaj(ألحجاج)

471
00:36:39,890 --> 00:36:44,247
in the story of Abdur Rahman Bin Muhammad Al-Ash'ath(عبد الرحمن بن محمدالاشعث) and Allah knows best.

472
00:36:44,701 --> 00:36:49,816
So, Ibn Hajar(ابن حجر) here is mentioning examples of those who revolted against unjust leaders

473
00:36:50,156 --> 00:36:54,618
and he mentioned Abdullah Bin Zubair(عبد الله بن زبير) and Hussain Ibn Ali(حسين بن علي) and the people of Madina

474
00:36:54,895 --> 00:36:57,881
and Abdur Rahman Ibn Ash'as(عبد الرحمن بن اشعث) as an examples.

475
00:36:58,729 --> 00:37:04,086
The people of Hawazin(هوازن), they sent a delegation to Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه

476
00:37:04,559 --> 00:37:08,882
asking Rasool Ullah to give them back their property because they lost everything.

477
00:37:09,261 --> 00:37:13,264
Their women and their children and their live stock was all gone.

478
00:37:13,415 --> 00:37:19,393
I mean, imagine an entire tribe, only the men are left and everything else is taken away from them.

479
00:37:19,897 --> 00:37:21,692
And this narration is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ)

480
00:37:21,985 --> 00:37:26,942
أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ، قَام حِينَ جَاءَهُ وَفْدُ هَوَازِنَ مُسْلِمِينَ

481
00:37:27,383 --> 00:37:31,682
 فَسَأَلُوهُ أَنْ يَرُدَّ إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوَالَهُمْ وَسَبْيَهُمْ

482
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:36,106
فَقَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : أَحَبُّ الحَدِيثِ إِلَيَّ أَصْدَقُهُ ،

483
00:37:36,503 --> 00:37:39,384
فَاخْتَارُوا إِحْدَى الطَّائِفَتَيْنِ ، إِمَّا السَّبْيَ وَإِمَّا المَالَ

484
00:37:39,719 --> 00:37:48,252
وَقَدْ كُنْتُ اسْتَأْنَيْتُ بِهِمْ ، وَقَدْ كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ انْتَظَرَ آخِرَهُمْ بِضْعَ عَشْرَةَ لَيْلَةً حِينَ قَفَلَ مِنَ الطَّائِفِ

485
00:37:48,381 --> 00:37:51,633
When Hawazin(هوازن) came to accept Islam

486
00:37:52,122 --> 00:37:56,930
they asked Rasool Allah ﷺ to return to them their wealth and their women and children.

487
00:37:57,104 --> 00:38:01,894
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: The most beloved words to me are the most truthful.

488
00:38:01,956 --> 00:38:06,402
So, choose one of two, either your women and children or the wealth.

489
00:38:06,544 --> 00:38:08,942
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them, I cannot give both back.

490
00:38:09,157 --> 00:38:11,609
I will give you either the women and children or the wealth.

491
00:38:12,031 --> 00:38:15,201
And I waited for you, so Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling them,

492
00:38:15,225 --> 00:38:18,794
I actually waited before distributing the Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

493
00:38:19,642 --> 00:38:22,792
With the hope that you would come to me, so I could give it back to you.

494
00:38:22,816 --> 00:38:24,339
But now it's already divided.

495
00:38:24,379 --> 00:38:29,170
I mean, it's already now within the property of Muslim individuals.

496
00:38:29,376 --> 00:38:31,585
So, I cannot take it away from them and give it back to you.

497
00:38:31,808 --> 00:38:34,134
But he told them choose one of the two.

498
00:38:34,253 --> 00:38:35,182
So, they said;

499
00:38:35,345 --> 00:38:38,944
If you are giving us the choice, then obviously, we're going to choose our woman and children.

500
00:38:39,317 --> 00:38:40,891
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

501
00:38:41,542 --> 00:38:45,729
I am going to give them back to you but I have to appeal to the Muslims.

502
00:38:46,301 --> 00:38:52,068
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ stood up in front of the Muslims. Praised Allahعَزّوجَلّ. And then said;

503
00:38:52,276 --> 00:38:56,965
أَمَّا بَعْدُ ، فَإِنَّ إِخْوَانَكُمْ هَؤُلاَءِ قَدْ جَاءُونَا تَائِبِينَ

504
00:38:57,399 --> 00:39:03,497
وَإِنِّي قَدْ رَأَيْتُ أَنْ أَرُدَّ إِلَيْهِمْ سَبْيَهُمْ مَنْ أَحَبَّ منكم أَنْ يُطَيِّبَ ،بذالك فَلْيَفْعَلْ

505
00:39:03,680 --> 00:39:10,660
وَمَنْ أَحَبَّ مِنْكُمْ أَنْ يَكُونَ عَلَى حَظِّهِ حَتَّى نُعْطِيَهُ إِيَّاهُ مِنْ أَوَّلِ مَا يُفِيءُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْنَا فَلْيَفْعَلْ

506
00:39:10,797 --> 00:39:16,692
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Your brothers have come repenting, they became Muslim.

507
00:39:17,165 --> 00:39:20,854
And I want to give back to them their women and children.

508
00:39:21,311 --> 00:39:28,589
So, whoever among you, would allow to give them back what belongs to them, then he should do so.

509
00:39:29,020 --> 00:39:31,720
And whoever wants to be compensated,

510
00:39:32,131 --> 00:39:35,921
then I will compensate them from the first Ghaneemah(غنيمه) that we get.

511
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:39,908
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling them, if you want to give them back what belongs to them

512
00:39:39,933 --> 00:39:40,992
then that is better do it.

513
00:39:41,023 --> 00:39:46,373
If you want to give it back with a promise of reimbursement for what you have given

514
00:39:46,405 --> 00:39:50,244
that I will do that from the first Ghaneemah(غنيمه) that I get after this battle.

515
00:39:50,576 --> 00:39:56,758
So, the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) in the narration of Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ), it says that they all gave it back

516
00:39:56,782 --> 00:40:02,101
but Ibn Is'haaq(إبن إسحاق) mentions, the scholars of Seerah(سيرة) say that the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) said;

517
00:40:02,226 --> 00:40:06,351
We would give up what we have, the Ansaar(أنْصَار) said the same,

518
00:40:06,375 --> 00:40:13,057
but then Al-Akrah Bin Habis(الاقرع بن حابس) stood and said: Me and my tribe will not give up, what we have.

519
00:40:13,327 --> 00:40:16,174
Oyeynah Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن) said: We will not give up what we have.

520
00:40:16,727 --> 00:40:21,124
And then Al-Abbas Bin Mardaas(العباس بن مرداس) said: We will not give up what we have.

521
00:40:21,296 --> 00:40:26,788
But then his tribe Bannu Sulaim(بَنُوسُلَيم) stood up and said: No! We are going to give up, what we have.

522
00:40:27,074 --> 00:40:28,121
So, Al-Abbas(العباس) told them,

523
00:40:28,161 --> 00:40:29,140
 وَهَنْتُمُوْنِيْ

524
00:40:29,507 --> 00:40:31,000
You have disgraced me.

525
00:40:31,482 --> 00:40:33,646
But they have done the right thing.

526
00:40:33,884 --> 00:40:37,281
Rasool Allah ﷺ appealed to the people to give it back.

527
00:40:37,662 --> 00:40:42,846
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I will not know, who has given back and who has not.

528
00:40:42,986 --> 00:40:48,018
So, let Urafa'a(عرفاء), Urfaa(عرفاء) are the Shuyookh(شيوخ) of the tribes, the leaders of the tribes.

529
00:40:48,326 --> 00:40:50,562
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Let them report to me.

530
00:40:50,919 --> 00:40:53,927
Who has given up what they have and who didn't.

531
00:40:54,343 --> 00:40:57,235
Anyway, the women and children were returned to Hawazin(هوازن).

532
00:40:57,747 --> 00:41:03,802
While the live stock was split, it says that every individual got 40 sheep.

533
00:41:03,985 --> 00:41:06,884
It tells you that there was a huge Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

534
00:41:08,307 --> 00:41:12,021
Malik Ibn Auf(مالك بن عوف) received a message from Rasool Allah ﷺ

535
00:41:12,494 --> 00:41:17,195
saying that if you become Muslim, I will give you, what belongs to you

536
00:41:17,219 --> 00:41:20,827
and on top of that, I will give you 100 camels.

537
00:41:21,278 --> 00:41:25,524
So, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف) sneaked out from At-Taef(ألطائف)

538
00:41:25,966 --> 00:41:32,020
and he was there when it was besieged and he carried on resisting, until that moment.

539
00:41:32,605 --> 00:41:38,181
So, now when he is told by Rasool Allah ﷺ that I will give you, your property back, he came and he accepted Islam,

540
00:41:38,465 --> 00:41:44,491
and then he lead an army from his people, who became Muslim, against the people of At-Taef(ألطائف).

541
00:41:45,120 --> 00:41:47,470
I mean, he is the one who started the war against Rasool Ullah.

542
00:41:47,494 --> 00:41:53,456
And now he became Muslim and he is fighting against the ones, whom he encouraged to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ in the first place.

543
00:41:53,701 --> 00:41:58,968
So, again it shows us how Rasool Allah ﷺ was winning the hearts of the people.

544
00:41:59,408 --> 00:42:02,032
Ka'ab Ibn Zuhair(كعب ابن زهير) also became Muslim.

545
00:42:02,072 --> 00:42:08,262
Ka'ab Ibn Zuhair(كعب ابن زهير) was one of the poets, who used to use their poetry against Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

546
00:42:09,743 --> 00:42:17,427
His brother sent him a message telling him that Rasool Allah ﷺ is executing the poets who spoke against him.

547
00:42:17,718 --> 00:42:22,320
So, you either come to him as Muslim or flee before you're killed.

548
00:42:22,481 --> 00:42:25,054
So, Ka'ab(كعب) was very worried about this.

549
00:42:25,419 --> 00:42:30,177
And he was concerned that he might be killed.

550
00:42:30,770 --> 00:42:35,045
And the people who were advising him, were causing him this fear.

551
00:42:35,221 --> 00:42:39,525
But anyway, he decided that he will give it a try and go back to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

552
00:42:39,549 --> 00:42:40,779
So, he went to Rasool Ullah

553
00:42:41,038 --> 00:42:43,161
and Rasool Allah ﷺ did not know him.

554
00:42:43,185 --> 00:42:47,521
So, he went to Rasool Allah and said: Ka'ab Ibn Zuhair(كعب ابن زهير) came to you repenting,

555
00:42:47,572 --> 00:42:51,716
 and he wants to become Muslim, do you accept his Islam, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes! Let him come.

556
00:42:52,078 --> 00:42:53,997
He said: I am Ka'ab Ibn Zuhair(كعب ابن زهير).

557
00:42:54,215 --> 00:42:57,272
Then he gave his Bay'ah(بيعة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

558
00:42:57,524 --> 00:43:03,111
And he stood up and gave a wonderful poem, praising Rasool Allah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

559
00:43:03,545 --> 00:43:08,366
And the story goes, that Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Sahabah(صحابه) to listen to this poem.

560
00:43:08,495 --> 00:43:11,347
And then Rasool Allah, gave him his cloak, Al-Burda(البرده)

561
00:43:11,570 --> 00:43:14,725
And it is this Burda(برده) according to the stories,

562
00:43:15,039 --> 00:43:18,265
that ended up in the hands of the Khulafa(خلافاء) of Bannu Abbas(بنوعباس).

563
00:43:18,413 --> 00:43:22,443
They considered it to be Baraka(بركة), because it's belongs to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

564
00:43:22,467 --> 00:43:25,981
and it would be handed down from one Khaleefah(خليفه) to the next.

565
00:43:26,329 --> 00:43:30,602
Also Rasool Allah ﷺ we are talking about the events that happened within that year.

566
00:43:30,755 --> 00:43:38,989
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent men from the tribe of Ahmas(أحمس) to Zul Khalsa(ذوالخلصه) to destroy it and they destroyed it.

567
00:43:39,029 --> 00:43:43,211
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ, was destroying all of the remnants of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة)

568
00:43:43,251 --> 00:43:47,864
 all of these false idols, Asnaam(إصنام) were being destroyed.

569
00:43:48,368 --> 00:43:55,720
And this was bringing an end to the false worship in the land of Hijaaz(حجاز) and the rest of the Arabian Peninsula.

570
00:43:55,943 --> 00:43:59,809
This is the end of the events of the eighth year of Hijrah(هحرة)

571
00:44:00,148 --> 00:44:04,459
In sha Allah Ta'ala(اِن شاء اهِي تعالى), we will move on to the next in our following session.

572
00:44:04,564 --> 00:44:09,511
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًاكَثِيْرَا

573
00:44:09,696 --> 00:44:12,194
وَالسلا م عليكم ورحمة الله  وبركاته

